##############Racial Special Abilities##############

#Cameroceras
Pressure Adaptation								KEY:Cameroceras ~ Pressure Adaptation						CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.CamerocerasRacialTrait																																		DESC:A cameroceras suffers no pressure damage at depths less than 1 mile, even if it is instantaneously moved to a different pressure.																																																																																																																		SOURCEPAGE:p.49

#Clockwork Familiar - Copied from ISI
Electricity										KEY:Clockwork Familiar ~ Electricity						CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClockworkFamiliarRacialAbility.SpecialAttack.Extraordinary																																	DESC:A clockwork familiar's bite does an additional 1d6 electricity damage.																																																																																																																												SOURCEPAGE:p.57
Item Installation									KEY:Clockwork Familiar ~ Item Installation					CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClockworkFamiliarRacialAbility.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary																																	DESC:Each clockwork familiar possesses the ability to carry a magic item in its body. This specific item type is chosen at the time of the construct's creation, and cannot be changed. While the creature cannot activate or use the item, it gains certain constant abilities from the resonant magic fields, and can drain the item's magic as a free action in order to gain additional magical effects. In addition, any clockwork construct can drain a single charge or spell level from its installed item to heal itself for 1d6 hit points as a standard action. Removing a spent item and installing a new one is a full-round action.																					BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Clockwork Familiar Installed Item Choice|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.57

Potion Installation								KEY:Clockwork Familiar ~ Potion Installation					CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClockworkFamiliarInstalledItem																																						DESC:The clockwork familiar gains a constant protection from good/evil/law/chaos effect (one type only, chosen each time a new potion is installed). In addition, a clockwork familiar can drain the magic from the potion in order to grant this ability to a creature sharing its space. This ability to include others in the protection effect lasts for 1 minute per spell level of the potion drained.																																																																						SOURCEPAGE:p.57
Scroll Installation								KEY:Clockwork Familiar ~ Scroll Installation					CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClockworkFamiliarInstalledItem																																						DESC:The clockwork familiar gains a constant detect magic effect as a spell-like ability. Draining magic from a scroll allows the familiar to cast a single identify spell on behalf of its master for each spell level of the spell inscribed on the scroll-these castings may be stored and saved, though a scroll used in this manner becomes instantly useless, even if not all spell levels have been drained.																																																																					SOURCEPAGE:p.57
Wand Installation									KEY:Clockwork Familiar ~ Wand Installation					CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClockworkFamiliarInstalledItem																																						DESC:The clockwork familiar gains the ability to spit a glob of acid up to 30 feet as a ranged touch attack, dealing 1d4 points of damage. Draining a charge increases the damage to 2d4 points for a single attack. This charge is spent before the attack is rolled.																																																																																													SOURCEPAGE:p.57

#Digmaul
Ball Tail										KEY:Digmaul ~ Ball Tail									CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.DigmaulRacialTrait																																			DESC:A digmaul has a spiked ball at the end of its tail, which it can use as a secondary natural attack that deals 1d4 points of bludgeoning and piercing damage. The digmaul can substitute a trip or bull rush combat maneuver check for its normal tail attack. Such a combat maneuver check doesn't provoke attacks of opportunity and receives a +4 racial bonus; a digmaul that fails its trip attempt by 10 or more in this way is not tripped.																																																															SOURCEPAGE:p.82

#Dinosaur (Plesiosaurus)
Ambush Attack									KEY:Plesiosaurus ~ Ambush Attack							CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.PlesiosaurusRacialTrait																																		DESC:If a plesiosaurus successfully hits a foe with its bite attack in the surprise round, it inflicts an additional 1d6 points of damage and threatens a critical hit on an 18-20. The additional damage from the ambush attack itself is precision damage and is not multiplied on a successful critical hit.																																																																																						SOURCEPAGE:p.83

#Dinosaur (Therizinosaurus)
Sprint										KEY:Therizinosaurus ~ Sprint								CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.TherizinosaurusRacialTrait																																	DESC:Once per hour, a therizinosaurus can move at 10 times its normal speed (400 feet) when it makes a charge.																																																																																																																						SOURCEPAGE:p.84
Sweeping Strike									KEY:Therizinosaurus ~ Sweeping Strike						CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.TherizinosaurusRacialTrait																																		DESC:As a full-round action, a therizinosaurus can hunker down and make a great, sweeping attack with its claws against up to four adjacent foes. The dinosaur makes an attack roll against each target, inflicting claw damage on a successful hit.																																																																																																SOURCEPAGE:p.84

#Dinosaur (Troodon)
Easily Trained									KEY:Troodon ~ Easily Trained								CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.TroodonRacialTrait																																			DESC:A troodon is unusually quick to pick up tricks and animal training. All Handle Animal checks made to train a troodon gain a +2 bonus. A troodon can learn an additional 2 tricks beyond what an animal of its intelligence can normally be taught.																																																																																				BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Animal Trick|2						SOURCEPAGE:p.84

#Kaprosuchus
Ramming Snout									KEY:Kaprosuchus ~ Ramming Snout							CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.KaprosuchusRacialTrait																																		DESC:When a kaprosuchus charges, it can ram an opponent with the calcified tip of its snout. This attack has the same attack bonus as the kaprosuchus's bite attack, and it deals an amount of bludgeoning damage equal to the kaprosuchus's bite damage. If the attack is successful, the kaprosuchus can attempt a trip combat maneuver against the target as a free action.																																																																											SOURCEPAGE:p.170

#Liminal Sprite
Repartee										KEY:Liminal Sprite ~ Repartee								CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.LiminalSpriteRacialTrait																																		DESC:Three times per day, when a liminal sprite successfully aids another creature's Charisma-based skill check, the creature gains a +2d4 bonus on the skill check instead of the normal +2 bonus. A creature can receive this bonus from only one liminal sprite per skill check.																																																																																										SOURCEPAGE:p.158
Versatile Performance								KEY:Liminal Sprite ~ Versatile Performance					CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.LiminalSpriteRacialTrait																																		DESC:A liminal sprite can use its bonus for Perform (comedy) in place of its bonus for Bluff and Intimidate. When substituting in this way, the liminal sprite uses its total bonus for Perform (comedy), including any class skill bonus, in place of the associated skill's total bonus, whether or not it has ranks in Perform (comedy) or Perform (comedy) is a class skill for the sprite.																																																																								SOURCEPAGE:p.158
Spell-Like Abilities								KEY:Liminal Sprite ~ SLA								CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.SpellLike.LiminalSpriteRacialTrait					SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=6|Daze,10+CHA|Prestidigitation	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=3|CASTERLEVEL=6|Fumbletongue,11+CHA|Invisibility (self only)|Memory Lapse,11+CHA

#Sahkil (Esipil)
Bewildering Assault								KEY:Esipil ~ Bewildering Assault							CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.EsipilRacialTrait																																			DESC:If an esipil makes a successful critical hit with one of its natural attacks, the target is confused for 1 round.																																																																																																																					SOURCEPAGE:p.213
Look of Fear									KEY:Esipil ~ Look of Fear								CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.EsipilRacialTrait																																			DESC:A creature affected by an esipil's gaze is shaken for 1 round.																																																																																																																													SOURCEPAGE:p.213	ASPECT:Ability Benefit|(30 ft., DC 14)
Spell-Like Abilities								KEY:Esipil ~ SLA										CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.SpellLike.EsipilRacialTrait							SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=3|Cause Fear,13+CHA|Mage Hand	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=3|CASTERLEVEL=3|Mirror Image	SPELLS:Innate|CASTERLEVEL=3|Contact Other Plane
CATEGORY=Special Ability|Change Shape.COPY=Esipil ~ Change Shape									OUTPUTNAME:Change Shape						TYPE:EsipilRacialTrait																																																																																																																																																																																			ASPECT:Ability Benefit|(tiny cat or dog; beast shape II)

#Whale (Narwhal)
Hold Breath										KEY:Narwhal ~ Hold Breath								CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.NarwhalRacialTrait																																			DESC:Narwhals are expert deep divers, and a narwhal can hold its breath %1 minutes equal to 2 times its Constitution score.|2*CONSCORE																																																																																																																		SOURCEPAGE:p.276
Tusk											KEY:Narwhal ~ Tusk									CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.NarwhalRacialTrait																																			DESC:A charging narwhal can make a single gore attack with its tusk in place of its normal bite attack. If it hits, the tusk deals 2d6+14 points of damage with a x3 critical multiplier.																																																																																																									SOURCEPAGE:p.276

#Whale (Blue)
Hold Breath										KEY:Blue Whale ~ Hold Breath								CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.BlueWhaleRacialTrait																																		DESC:A blue whale can hold its breath for %1 minutes before it risks drowning.|10*CONSCORE																																																																																																																									SOURCEPAGE:p.276

#Wolliped
Spit											KEY:Wolliped ~ Spit									CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.WollipedRacialTrait																																			DESC:Once per hour, a wolliped can regurgitate the contents of its stomach, spitting the foul slurry at a single target within 10 feet as a ranged touch attack. On a successful hit, the target must succeed at a DC %1 Fortitude save or be sickened for 1d4 rounds.|12+CHA																																																																																												SOURCEPAGE:p.279

#Wysp
Living Battery									KEY:Wysp ~ Living Battery								CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.WyspRacialTrait																																			DESC:As an immediate action, a wysp can kill itself to cause a creature benefiting from its resonance to heal 2 hit points for each of that creature's HD. If the wysp uses this ability, its death can't be prevented, and its life can't be restored by any effect less than true resurrection, miracle, or wish, even if such an effect can normally revive an outsider.																																																																											SOURCEPAGE:p.282
Resonance										KEY:Wysp ~ Resonance									CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.WyspRacialTrait.Aura																																		DESC:A wysp's natural resonance strengthens the power of its element. The wysp grants a +2 competence bonus on attack rolls and damage rolls to all creatures within 30 feet with an elemental subtype that matches the wysp's, and to the DCs of all racial spell-like, supernatural, and extraordinary abilities of such creatures (as usual, this does not include creatures assuming an elemental form). Kineticists within 30 feet who share the wysp's element gain a +1 competence bonus on attack rolls and damage rolls. The wysp's statistics already include these bonuses.																																									SOURCEPAGE:p.282
Servitor										KEY:Wysp ~ Servitor									CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.WyspRacialTrait																																			DESC:A wysp is a natural servitor. When it uses the aid another action to assist a creature benefiting from its resonance, the wisp can grant that creature a +4 bonus instead of +2. No other effect can increase this bonus beyond +4.																																																																																																		SOURCEPAGE:p.282

#Wysp (Aether)
Lesser Telekinesis								KEY:Aether Wysp ~ Lesser Telekinesis						CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.AetherWyspRacialTrait																																		DESC:By extending its strands of aether, an aether wysp can move small objects at a distance, as per mage hand except that lesser telekinesis is a supernatural ability and can move magical or nonmagical objects weighing up to 10 pounds.																																																																																																	SOURCEPAGE:p.282

#Wysp (Water)
Drench										KEY:Water Wysp ~ Drench									CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.WaterWyspRacialTrait																																			DESC:A water wysp's touch puts out Large or smaller nonmagical flames. The creature can dispel magical fire it touches as per dispel magic (caster level = the wysp's HD).																																																																																																											SOURCEPAGE:p.283

#Xiao
Spell-Like Abilities								KEY:Xiao ~ SLA										CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.SpellLike.XiaoRacialTrait							SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=3|CASTERLEVEL=3|Burning Hands,11+CHA|Spark

